WEBVTT

00:03:29.511 --> 00:03:33.067
And they got together to work on this manuscript.

00:03:33.067 --> 00:03:36.878
The first problem was a conservation problem.

00:03:36.878 --> 00:03:39.311
And this is the sort of thing that we had to deal with:

00:03:39.311 --> 00:03:41.511
There was glue on the spine of the book.

00:03:41.511 --> 00:03:43.712
And if you look at this photograph carefully,

00:03:43.712 --> 00:03:45.760
the bottom half of this is rather brown.

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:47.128
And that glue is hide glue.

00:03:47.128 --> 00:03:48.513
Now if you're a conservator,

00:03:48.513 --> 00:03:50.645
you can take off this glue reasonably easily.

00:03:50.645 --> 00:03:54.010
The top half is Elmer's wood glue.

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:56.127
It's polyvinyl acetate emulsion

00:03:56.127 --> 00:03:58.794
that doesn't dissolve in water once it's dry.

00:03:58.794 --> 00:04:01.960
And it's much tougher than the parchment that it was written on.